      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "636bedcbbf10b44259f3fb71",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Before the new main menu was introduced, avatars built with the \"Build & Test\" option for local testing, would appear in the \"Other\" category pretty much immediately. However since the new menu was added, this no longer seems to be the case.\nThe only way that I can seem to reliably get newly built avatars to show up in the \"Other\" category, is by restarting the game. \nAs it is rather time consuming to have to restart the game each time I want to test, it would be fantastic if this past behaviour was brought back.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[Build 1249] Avatars built with \"Build & Test\" do not appear in new main menu until restart.",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "631a4ce19b6ea744a6e76f83",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "_id": "63728bfab5fff444a5bc1866",
      "author": {
        "_id": "62fbd306dbae6a44a9f7423d",
        "alias": "Proper Raven",
        "aliasID": "65c27fc1ed6eefce4c3a481d",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/385fd548f4093771d31c1774ce854de2.png",
        "created": "2022-08-16T17:25:26.950Z",
        "name": "Campa",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "boardID": "58c62f2b3cf8f8367753b2f0",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-11-14T18:42:02.089Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "63728bfab5fff444a5bc1866",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Whenever I click publish for an avatar, the avatar will not show up in the menu no matter what I do unless I close and relaunch the game. I've tried switching avatars back and forth, switching worlds, waiting for hours, nothing will update the menu.\nThis has been happening for a good while now, and it's quite obnoxious how much this slows down testing, I've resorted to changing the name and color of something on the avatar just to make sure that updated avatars are clearly loading the updated version and not the old one, which it will never load the new one until I restart the game. \nSame thing seems to happen for build and test seen in this post: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/build-1249-avatars-built-with-build-test-do-not-appear-in-new-main-menu-until-re",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Updated or new avatar doesn't appear in menu until restarting vrchat",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "631a4ce19b6ea744a6e76f83",
      "private": false,
